Trace polymorphic array processing across the inheritance hierarchy. What does this code print?

```java
class AccountRecord {
    int getFee() { return 5; }
}
class GoldRecord extends AccountRecord {
    int getFee() { return 2; }
}
class PlatinumRecord extends AccountRecord {
    int getFee() { return 0; }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        AccountRecord[] list = { new AccountRecord(), new GoldRecord(), new PlatinumRecord() };
        int sum = 0;
        for (AccountRecord a : list) {
            sum += a.getFee();
        }
        System.out.println(sum);
    }
}
```

What is printed by the following safe downcasting pattern using pattern matching with instanceof?

```java
class SensorHub {}
class TemperatureSensor extends SensorHub {
    int reading = 72;
}
class PressureSensor extends SensorHub {
    int reading = 30;
}
public class Main {
    static void process(SensorHub hub) {
        if (hub instanceof TemperatureSensor t) {
            System.out.print(t.reading + " ");
        } else if (hub instanceof PressureSensor p) {
            System.out.print(p.reading + " ");
        }
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        process(new TemperatureSensor());
        process(new PressureSensor());
    }
}
```

